affiliation": "Department of Molecular Biology, Graduate School of Pharmaceutical Sciences, Nagoya City University, Nagoya, Aichi, Japan."}]}}, {"fullName": "Maki H", "lastName": "Maki", "firstName": "Honoka", "initials": "H", "authorId": {"type": "ORCID", "value": "0009-0007-0484-8657"}, "authorAffiliationDetailsList": {"authorAffiliation": [{"affiliation": "Department of Molecular Biology, Graduate School of Pharmaceutical Sciences, Nagoya City University, Nagoya, Aichi, Japan."}]}}, {"fullName": "Shirane M", "lastName": "Shirane", "firstName": "Michiko", "initials": "M", "authorId": {"type": "ORCID", "value": "0000-0002-8297-9245"}, "authorAffiliationDetailsList": {"authorAffiliation": [{"affiliation": "Department of Molecular Biology, Graduate School of Pharmaceutical Sciences, Nagoya City University, Nagoya, Aichi, Japan."}]}}]}, "authorIdList": {"authorId": [{"type": "ORCID", "value": "0000-0002-8297-9245"}, {"type": "ORCID", "value": "0009-0005-0242-9438"}, {"type": "ORCID", "value": "0009-0007-0484-8657"}]}, "dataLinksTagsList": {"dataLinkstag": ["supporting_data"]}, "journalInfo": {"issue": "4", "volume": "27", "journalIssueId": 4292313, "dateOfPublication": "2026 Dec", "monthOfPublication": 12, "yearOfPublication": 2026, "journal": {"medlineAbbreviation": "Traffic", "title": "Traffic (Copenhagen, Denmark)", "essn": "1600-0854", "issn": "1398-9219", "nlmid": "100939340", "isoabbreviation": "Traffic"}, "printPublicationDate": "2026-12-01"}, "pubYear": "2026", "pageInfo": "e70057", "abstractText": "At membrane contact sites (MCSs) between the endoplasmic reticulum (ER) and endolysosomal compartments, the Protrudin-PDZD8 complex promotes the maturation of endosomes into lysosomes, a process accompanied by acidification. Endosomal maturation is closely associated with both lysosomal acidification and calcium signaling; however, the molecular mechanisms linking the Protrudin-PDZD8 complex to these processes remain unclear. Here, we identified TMEM55B, a lysosome-localized protein, as a binding partner of the Protrudin-PDZD8 complex. TMEM55B has been reported to interact with the v-ATPase complex, suggesting a role in lysosomal function. Suppression of TMEM55B expression reduced the fluorescence of a lysosomal acidification probe, suggesting impaired lysosomal acidification. In addition, TMEM55B depletion attenuated lysosomal Ca<sup>2+</sup> release and reuptake and reduced ATP-induced Ca<sup>2+</sup> responses in the ER. These findings suggest impaired calcium-induced calcium release (CICR) at ER-lysosome MCSs. By contrast, mitochondrial Ca<sup>2+</sup> dynamics were unaffected. Together, these results identify TMEM55B as a factor involved in maintaining lysosomal homeostasis and regulating calcium dynamics. Our findings suggest that TMEM55B cooperates with the Protrudin-PDZD8 complex to contribute to the regulation of lysosomal function at ER-lysosome MCSs.", "affiliation": "Department of Molecular Biology, Graduate School of Pharmaceutical Sciences, Nagoya City University, Nagoya, Aichi, Japan.", "publicationStatus": "ppublish", "language": "eng", "pubModel": "Print", "pubTypeList": {"pubType": ["research-article", "Journal Article"]}, "grantsList": {"grant": [{"agency": "Japan Society for the Promotion of Science", "grantId": "24K02122", "orderIn": 0}, {"agency": "Japan Society for the Promotion of Science", "grantId": "JPMJSP2130", "orderIn": 0}]}, "meshHeadingList": {"meshHeading": [{"majorTopic_YN": "N", "descriptorName": "Hela Cells"}, {"majorTopic_YN": "Y", "descriptorName": "Lysosomes", "meshQualifierList": {"meshQualifier": [{"majorTopic_YN": "N", "abbreviation": "ME", "qualifierName": "metabolism"}]}}, {"majorTopic_YN": "Y", "descriptorName": "Endoplasmic Reticulum", "meshQualifierList": {"meshQualifier": [{"majorTopic_YN": "N", "abbreviation": "ME", "qualifierName": "metabolism"}]}}, {"majorTopic_YN": "N", "descriptorName": "Animals"}, {"majorTopic_YN": "N", "descriptorName": "Humans"}, {"majorTopic_YN": "N", "